 "notes": [
  "Same start as Case A (identical positions at t=0, verified by the tests).",
  "X5 reads the cut and jumps out early (1.1 s) around O5 toward the top to take O2 away; X2 keeps chasing O2 through the corridor, so two defenders end up on the shooter.",
  "X1 also overplays the perimeter pass (steps into the lane toward the top).",
  "O5 reads X5 leaving BEFORE any screen contact (1.35 s) and slips down the right side of the lane; he never closes the door.",
  "O4 pops to the left slot to keep X4 busy; O3 stays in the corner; X3 rotates from the weak side but arrives late.",
  "O1 picks up the dribble, steps down with the ball and throws a bounce pass past X1's low hip (1.95-2.45 s); O5 finishes with a layup."
